The natural planted family fails the hardness screen for a fundamental reason. In the paper’s classical guaranteed regime, \(|A|\) is tiny compared with the least prime divisor \(p\); for a planted set drawn without special algebraic structure, almost every permutation avoids the \(O(n^2)\) possible zero-sum intervals. I’m quantifying that with the required structure-aware sampler (uniform permutations of the supplied set), rather than using the misleading \(k^n\) space.
